 Re-derive the evidence_sufficient consumer inventory via find_referencing_symbols + a name-string grep, and reconcile it with AC5: list close_precheck._verification_fail_message (:436/441) explicitly (it is the failure surface AC5 changes, not an untouched consumer), plus _cli/_llm_commands.py:675 and audit/page.py:314.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5426,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan text: 'Existing consumers of the signal (completion_reconcile derivation :198, _insufficiency_only :115, completion_sidecar payload passthrough :382, completion_tool_policy, the finalizer prompt's banked-evidence rule) are enumerated in the change and stay untouched'","grep `evidence_sufficient`: src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:441 `if result.get(\"evidence_sufficient\") is False:` inside `_verification_fail_message` — an unlisted consumer in the modified file","AC5: 'Still exhausted after the bounded resumptions -> the existing failure surface, with the message stating auto-resume was attempted N times' — this edits _verification_fail_message, contradicting its listing as untouched","grep also: src/rebar/_cli/_llm_commands.py:675 and src/rebar/audit/page.py:314 read the same marker and are absent from the inventory"],"finding":"The plan's enumerated inventory of 'existing consumers of the [evidence_sufficient] signal ... [that] stay untouched' is incomplete: it omits `_verification_fail_message` (src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py:436/441), which reads `result.get('evidence_sufficient')` and lives in the exact file the resumption loop modifies. This consumer is the 'existing failure surface' AC5 requires to change ('the message stating auto-resume was attempted N times'), so listing it as untouched is self-contradictory. The sweep also omits the CLI consumer `_cli/_llm_commands.py:675` and the audit renderer `audit/page.py:314`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3a7f63ae97ebef1a","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Mechanism step 2: 'Existing consumers of the signal (completion_reconcile derivation :198, _insufficiency_only :115, completion_sidecar payload passthrough :382, completion_tool_policy, the finalizer prompt's banked-evidence rule) are enumerated in the change and stay untouched'","norm_id":"n0bde3b22ee59db27","priority":0.3574,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["_verification_fail_message (close_precheck.py:436-450): if treated as untouched, the AC5 'auto-resume attempted N times' message has nowhere to land, or the author edits it unplanned — an in-file consumer the inventory declared out of scope","_cli/_llm_commands.py:675: the CLI verify-completion output consumer of evidence_sufficient — unlisted, so a behavior/format change here would be unaudited","audit/page.py:314: the ticket audit-page renderer of the per-criterion marker — unlisted; the AC6 'resumption trail visible on the ticket' interacts with this render path"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6667,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether raised exhaustion (LLMBudgetExhaustedError / token-cap bubbling out at close_precheck.py:646) is in scope for auto-resume; if in scope, classify it as insufficiency-only at the exception arm too, and if out of scope, say so explicitly and confirm the recovery orchestrator ALWAYS finalizes a returned FAIL verdict for the motivating exhaustion path.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3067,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["close_precheck.py:646 `except Exception as exc: ... raise CommandError(... completion verification could not run ...)` — a raised exhaustion never reaches the verdict-inspection at :676","completion_recovery.py:325-330 catches LLMBudgetExhaustedError/RunawayToolLoopError and returns a finalized FAIL verdict — so the returned-verdict path exists ONLY when recovery is engaged","Plan step 2 keys entirely on `_insufficiency_only(result)` over the returned verdict; no handling stated for the raised-exhaustion arm"],"finding":"The plan's classification seam inspects only the RETURNED verdict (_insufficiency_only on result), but budget/token exhaustion can also surface as a RAISED exception (LLMBudgetExhaustedError / token-cap) that bubbles out of verify_completion and is converted to a CommandError at close_precheck.py:646-674 before any verdict inspection — the recovery orchestrator catches exhaustion and finalizes a FAIL verdict (completion_recovery.py:325-330) only when recovery is engaged. The plan does not state whether a raised exhaustion is in scope; if it is not, auto-resume silently never fires for closes where exhaustion raises rather than returns.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f433b284bb84048ea","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Mechanism step 1 & 2 (close_precheck._completion_precheck seam; classification via _insufficiency_only)","norm_id":"n44e669a530562be4","prio